1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,128
A wrong approval hurts a patient. An extra hold costs a reviewer one minute.

2
00:00:07,228 --> 00:00:13,231
Everything you are about to see follows from that one asymmetry.

3
00:00:13,331 --> 00:00:16,802
MedCheck reads a free text case note.

4
00:00:16,902 --> 00:00:22,154
It returns exactly one verdict: approve, hold, or block.

5
00:00:22,254 --> 00:00:26,381
But the interesting part is not the verdict.

6
00:00:26,481 --> 00:00:31,171
It is that the model is not allowed to produce it.

7
00:00:31,271 --> 00:00:37,555
And we can prove that offline, in eight seconds, without a network,

8
00:00:37,655 --> 00:00:40,000
and without an A P I key.

9
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:43,271
Three cases. Three verdicts.

10
00:00:43,371 --> 00:00:51,547
The first is warfarin at five milligrams, with normal kidney function.

11
00:00:51,647 --> 00:00:56,086
Every check passes, so it is approved.

12
00:00:56,186 --> 00:01:03,312
Notice that the approval itself is a finding with a rule i d.

13
00:01:03,412 --> 00:01:08,084
It is not a sentence written by a model.

14
00:01:08,184 --> 00:01:13,557
The second is simvastatin plus clarithromycin.

15
00:01:13,657 --> 00:01:21,016
The table marks that pair as contraindicated, so it is blocked.

16
00:01:21,116 --> 00:01:27,307
And the reason names the rule: D D I zero zero seven.

17
00:01:27,407 --> 00:01:32,547
The third is the one I want you to remember.

18
00:01:32,647 --> 00:01:37,787
Digoxin, one hundred twenty five micrograms.

19
00:01:37,887 --> 00:01:43,961
And the note never says what the kidney function is.

20
00:01:44,061 --> 00:01:51,537
The system does not approve it. And it does not block it either.

21
00:01:51,637 --> 00:01:59,112
Blocking would mean: this dose is too high. We do not know that.

22
00:01:59,212 --> 00:02:07,039
What we know is that we cannot evaluate it. So the verdict is hold.

23
00:02:07,139 --> 00:02:13,447
And the finding says exactly that: renal data missing.

24
00:02:13,547 --> 00:02:21,139
That distinction is the whole design. Hold is not an error state.

25
00:02:21,239 --> 00:02:30,000
Hold is the system telling the truth about the limits of its own knowledge.

26
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:33,573
These three pairs are not mock ups.

27
00:02:33,673 --> 00:02:38,266
Each one is a real defect from our bug diary.

28
00:02:38,366 --> 00:02:44,287
And each one can be reproduced by removing a single guard.

29
00:02:44,387 --> 00:02:51,124
On the left of the first pair, the coverage check is switched off.

30
00:02:51,224 --> 00:02:55,817
Metformin plus ciprofloxacin becomes approve.

31
00:02:55,917 --> 00:03:02,144
Because not in the table was silently read as no interaction.

32
00:03:02,244 --> 00:03:05,306
That is the fail open mistake.

33
00:03:05,406 --> 00:03:12,756
And it is the reason the table now declares unassessed pairs explicitly.

34
00:03:12,856 --> 00:03:22,655
In the middle, the old behaviour banded a missing kidney function as the most conservative band,

35
00:03:22,755 --> 00:03:28,165
and then compared against it. So digoxin was blocked.

36
00:03:28,265 --> 00:03:34,186
Blocking was the safer sounding answer, and the wrong one.

37
00:03:34,286 --> 00:03:41,533
On the right, our own gate. It asked whether the ledger named an A D R.

38
00:03:41,633 --> 00:03:43,981
And the answer was yes,

39
00:03:44,081 --> 00:03:49,797
because the baseline A D R had been there since day one.

40
00:03:49,897 --> 00:03:56,226
A frozen contract was rewritten, and all six gates went green.

41
00:03:56,326 --> 00:04:00,409
We fixed the gate, not the pull request.

42
00:04:00,509 --> 00:04:06,838
Every one of these was found by a machine disagreeing with us.

43
00:04:06,938 --> 00:04:10,000
Not by reading code carefully.

44
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:13,896
None of these is a business feature.

45
00:04:13,996 --> 00:04:20,599
They are constraints that make a class of mistake impossible.

46
00:04:20,699 --> 00:04:29,032
And each has a test that fails when you delete it. First, the authority seam.

47
00:04:29,132 --> 00:04:37,142
The extraction contract has no field for a verdict, a severity, or a dose.

48
00:04:37,242 --> 00:04:43,952
A model cannot author one, because there is nowhere to put it.

49
00:04:44,052 --> 00:04:49,572
This is not a prompt that asks the model to behave.

50
00:04:49,672 --> 00:04:57,248
It is a type that gives it no vocabulary. Second, the structural rule.

51
00:04:57,348 --> 00:05:03,734
The perception layer may not import the adjudication layer.

52
00:05:03,834 --> 00:05:09,679
If someone tried to let the extractor see the verdict,

53
00:05:09,779 --> 00:05:18,004
the build would fail before review. Third, the table declares its own holes.

54
00:05:18,104 --> 00:05:23,408
Absence of a pair means assessed, no interaction.

55
00:05:23,508 --> 00:05:30,110
It does not mean we never looked. Those are different claims.

56
00:05:30,210 --> 00:05:34,431
And only one of them is safe to act on.

57
00:05:34,531 --> 00:05:41,458
Together, these give us a property we can state in one sentence.

58
00:05:41,558 --> 00:05:50,000
No output of this system can assert a conclusion that the code did not derive.

59
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:57,375
Traceability here is not a spreadsheet somebody maintains. It is enforced.

60
00:05:57,475 --> 00:06:00,365
Every requirement has an i d.

61
00:06:00,465 --> 00:06:07,641
Every test docstring must name the requirement or invariant it verifies.

62
00:06:07,741 --> 00:06:13,123
And a structural test fails the build if one does not.

63
00:06:13,223 --> 00:06:16,611
That is why the matrix cannot rot.

64
00:06:16,711 --> 00:06:23,986
The cheapest way to add a test is also the compliant way. Then the agent.

65
00:06:24,086 --> 00:06:28,272
The agent reads A G E N T S dot M D first.

66
00:06:28,372 --> 00:06:32,857
And that file tells it what it may not touch.

67
00:06:32,957 --> 00:06:38,837
The permission model is deny by default: no read, no write,

68
00:06:38,937 --> 00:06:45,415
unless a path is explicitly listed. Nine surfaces are human only.

69
00:06:45,515 --> 00:06:49,601
Including the rules that judge the agent.

70
00:06:49,701 --> 00:06:53,788
The launch prompt is not build me an app.

71
00:06:53,888 --> 00:07:01,661
It is: produce an execution plan with traceability, interface contract, scope,

72
00:07:01,761 --> 00:07:06,844
and test strategy. Then stop, and wait for a human.

73
00:07:06,944 --> 00:07:14,419
In our transcripts, thirty interventions were recorded. Six were approvals.

74
00:07:14,519 --> 00:07:20,000
The other twenty four changed what the agent was doing.

75
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:29,228
Six gates. All blocking. Test approval. Static analysis. Requirements schema.

76
00:07:29,328 --> 00:07:38,675
Semantic evaluation. Regression. And the A I use log. The last one is unusual.

77
00:07:38,775 --> 00:07:48,242
If you change code or a prompt, without recording the session that produced it,

78
00:07:48,342 --> 00:07:53,495
the build fails. That gate caught us twice.

79
00:07:53,595 --> 00:08:01,624
And both times, we added the record, instead of loosening the gate.

80
00:08:01,724 --> 00:08:08,555
The gate you just saw fail is the fix for our own defect.

81
00:08:08,655 --> 00:08:15,965
A change to a frozen contract must now add or amend an A D R,

82
00:08:16,065 --> 00:08:23,855
in the same change. Citation of an old decision no longer counts.

83
00:08:23,955 --> 00:08:28,868
And the invariants are not just asserted.

84
00:08:28,968 --> 00:08:34,121
Two of the five have been mutation checked.

85
00:08:34,221 --> 00:08:39,494
Delete the guard, and a named test goes red.

86
00:08:39,594 --> 00:08:46,305
The other three are recorded as debt, with a task sheet,

87
00:08:46,405 --> 00:08:50,000
rather than described as done.

88
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:54,743
Three things are not done. And they are written down, rather than hidden.

89
00:08:54,843 --> 00:08:58,611
The live model path has never been measured on real notes.

90
00:08:58,711 --> 00:09:00,335
That field is still null.

91
00:09:00,435 --> 00:09:04,008
Three of five invariants have no mutation evidence yet.

92
00:09:04,108 --> 00:09:07,941
And the transcripts are reconstructions from the build log,

93
00:09:08,041 --> 00:09:09,990
awaiting member certification.

94
00:09:10,090 --> 00:09:15,092
A safety claim is only worth the list of things you admit you have not shown.

95
00:09:15,192 --> 00:09:20,000
A system that can refuse is more trustworthy than one that always answers.

